ael-rey"],"publicationYear":2011,"pageCount":303,"summary":"\"The fall of the Ottoman and Russian empires were watershed events in modern history. The unraveling of these empires was both cause and consequence of World War I and resulted in the deaths of millions. It irrevocably changed the landscape of the Middle East and Eurasia and reverberates to this day in conflicts throughout the Caucasus and Middle East. Shattering Empires draws on extensive research in the Ottoman and Russian archives to tell the story of the rivalry and collapse of two great empires. Overturning accounts that portray their clash as one of conflicting nationalisms, this pioneering study argues that geopolitical competition and the emergence of a new global interstate order provide the key to understanding the course of history in the Ottoman-Russian borderlands in the twentieth century.","thumbnailUrl":"/book-covers/book-shattering-empires-the-clash-and-collapse-of-the-ottoman-and-russian-empires-1908-18-michael-rey.jpg","libraryShelf":{"scheme":"lcc","callNumber":"DR479 .R9 R49 2011","rawCallNumber":"DR479.R9 R49 2011","mainClass":"D","subclass":"DR","completeness":"full_call_number","confidence":"high","matchedBy":"open_library_exact_isbn","sourceId":"source-open-library-lcc-shattering-empires-the-clash-and-collapse-of-the-ottoman-and-russian-empires-1908-18-michael-rey","sourceEditionId":"/books/OL24892967M","sourceWorkId":"/works/OL15988330W","sourceIsbn13":"9780521195539","sort":{"classLetters":"DR","classWholeNumber":479,"cutters":[{"letters":"R","decimalDigits":"9"},{"letters":"R","decimalDigits":"49"}],"year":2011}},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[],"centralPlaces":[],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"The rivalry and collapse of the Ottoman and Russian empires in their borderlands are best explained by geopolitical competition and the emergence of a new global interstate order, rather than conflicting nationalisms.","confidence":0.8},"academicOrientation":{"sc